y guides their actions, and I'm carefully considering how A-FDT will impact the expected outcomes.\n\n\n**Examining Counterfactuals**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the implications of symmetric setups within A-FDT. The core dilemma lies in how counterfactual dependence plays out when identical agents, like our LLM instances, are in a Prisoner's Dilemma. I'm carefully considering how the essay's insights on calculators computing jointly apply to the prisoners, especially in situations where personal information differs while the underlying decision process remains identical.\n\n\n**Investigating Functional Dependence**\n\nI'm now diving into the functional dependence within this setup, specifically focusing on how the differing observations impact the LLM's decision function. My question is how A-FDT handles these distinctions when the model weights and reasoning remain identical. Given the different private leads and letter contents, but shared objective and sentencing, I need to understand if the observations act as a conditional that makes the agent defect.\n\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":1}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8201,"completion_tokens":793,"total_tokens":8994,"cost":0.0091245,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0091245,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00615075,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00297375},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":790,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}